Upon returning (according to gpt)
```
git switch / checkout main
git fetch
git pull origin main
git branch -d myBranch #kill old branch if needed
git checkout -b newBranch #make ur new branch



# make new changes
git add file
git commit -m "Describe what changed"
git push -u origin HEAD #push my current branch to the remote using the same branch name



#If your team uses a fork, the command may instead be:
git pull upstream main

```
